From c8ca18aa63436fd3090c8780c76669d0bc0b2a99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:51:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] build: Qt 4.8 support in qmake files and a src/qt4
 compatibility layer

Gate everything Qt 5-only in the qmake files behind the Qt major version:
-std=gnu++17 and a force-included src/qt4/qt4compat.h for Qt4 (qmake 2.01a
ignores CONFIG+=c++17), no QMAKE_MAC_SDK=macosx with Qt4's qmake, no
qmake-time lupdate run, QT+=widgets/no_testcase_installs only from Qt5 on,
and hand-quoted paths in the icon install rule, which uses $$shell_quote()
that qmake 2.01a does not know. Translations: Qt4 has no
lrelease/embed_translations features, so an updateqm extra compiler writes
localization/*.qm next to the .ts files and a checked-in localization.qrc
embeds them (same for the locale test).

src/qt4/ carries the Qt5 APIs the sources use that Qt4 lacks, under the Qt5
header names so the includes stay untouched: QRegularExpression (backed by
QRegExp, MultilineOption emulated line by line, implicit conversion to
QRegExp so the QString members accept it), QSaveFile, QTemporaryDir,
QStandardPaths, QRandomGenerator (/dev/urandom), QUrlQuery, QSignalBlocker,
QScopeGuard, QMessageAuthenticationCode with a byte-order-explicit SHA-256 /
SHA-512, plus qt4compat.h (QStringLiteral, qsizetype, Qt::SkipEmptyParts,
qEnvironmentVariable*) and qtestcompat.h (QTRY_*, one-argument QSKIP,
QTest::qWaitFor, qCompare against nullptr, a no-op
QTEST_SET_MAIN_SOURCE_PATH, and the QRegularExpression form of
QTest::ignoreMessage() through a chained message handler). FunctorThread
replaces QThread::create() on every Qt version. All of it is a no-op on
Qt >= 5.

